# #5837: the reachability latch exemption and the split transfer's link obligation.
MODULE: UnlinkedNeverClaimsPendingDonorCloseMarksProven
TARGET: UnlinkedNeverClaims
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the exemption marks an unlinked L proven; the gate flips to eager and L's first stamped write claims an epoch no owner replays (a5e2e2ef's condition 1)
PERTURBS: ProveReach
BOUNDS: WithFreeAdvance = TRUE, WithSplitBirth = TRUE, WithKeyMove = TRUE, MaxWindows = 1, WithMixedVersion = FALSE, WithDuplicate = FALSE, WithLatch = TRUE

--- FIND
    /\ lat' = IF moved THEN "proven" ELSE IF ExemptPending THEN "undecided" ELSE "latched"
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the exemption proves.
    /\ lat' = IF moved THEN "proven" ELSE IF ExemptPending THEN "proven" ELSE "latched"
--- END
